{
  "cdmVersionRange": ">=5.0.0",
  "_README": [
    "Ambulatory deficit / impaired ambulation. Serves BOTH the Iannuzzi",
    "ambu_deficit item (3 points) and the Kraiss sVQI-FS nonambulatory item",
    "(1 point) - identical 7-concept sets under two score-specific names, so one",
    "cohort backs both. covariates/cohort_map.csv maps both items here.",
    "",
    "THREE primary criteria, one per OMOP domain. This is the declarative",
    "replacement for the pipeline's domain = \"auto\" cross-domain union:",
    "  Observation      4012645 walking aid use, 437643 abnormal gait,",
    "                   439405 walking disability, 36714126 difficulty walking,",
    "                   4044714 using wheelchair",
    "  Procedure        4085915 provision of long cane",
    "  Device           4240470 wheelchair",
    "This is the highest-risk translation in the repo: querying a single domain",
    "returned 0 of 225 patients in pad-amp-nhd-val. Validate against",
    "query_auto_domain_covariate_counts() before trusting any score using it.",
    "",
    "includeDescendants mirrors the CSV exactly - TRUE for the four rollup",
    "concepts, FALSE for the three leaf concepts.",
    "PrimaryCriteriaLimit / QualifiedLimit / ExpressionLimit are all \"All\" and EndStrategy is StartDate+0, unlike the [DVI] VA-FI cohorts (1797948-1797977) which are \"First\". A first-ever-only cohort cannot answer a lookback-window question.",
    "",
    "2026-08-03 CLINICAL DECISION: 4240470 Wheelchair now includeDescendants=true,",
    "so all wheelchair types count (manual, power-assisted, motorized, bariatric,",
    "sports, pediatric, transport, stand-up, stair-climbing -- 136 concepts).",
    "Mirrors the same change in covariates/covariate_concepts*.csv; the regression",
    "test's concept-set drift check requires the two to agree.",
    "The subtree also contains parts and accessories (tire, lap tray, umbrella",
    "holder, 45767832 Wheelchair accessory), which therefore also activate the",
    "component -- accepted because a parts record still implies wheelchair use."
  ],
